  Headline: Added selection-based local masks, letting you grade just part of a photo or clip.
  Added    Local selections and masks: use lasso, polygon, rectangle, ellipse, brush and colour-range tools to isolate part of a picture or clip, then combine them with add/subtract/intersect, feather, grow and invert. A selection becomes a named, hideable mask with its own grade (colour, curves, LUT, power window, plugin), stored at full picture resolution — either on a photo or as a static matte on a video clip.
  Added    The brush selection tool now has an explicit Add/Remove switch, so you can erase part of a selection with the brush without needing to hold a modifier key (handy on systems where Alt+drag is already taken by the window manager).
  Improved When editing a mask, the clip panel now hides controls that a mask ignores (fades, reframe, keyframes), making clear which settings actually apply while a mask is selected.
  Fixed    The incoming clip of a transition now renders with its own masks applied during preview, instead of showing an unmasked picture.

